calling f before visiting each node. Each call to f provides the current node and traversal stack,
consisting of the original value of stack appended with all nodes
from root to n, excluding n itself. (This design allows calls
to PreorderStack to be nested without double counting.) If f returns false, the traversal skips over that subtree. Unlike Inspect , no second call to f is made after visiting node n.
(In practice, the second call is nearly always used only to pop the
stack, and it is surprisingly tricky to do this correctly.) func Print ¶ func Print(fset * token . FileSet , x any ) error Print prints x to standard output, skipping nil fields.
